Local changes to OpenJarvis used by Akira Assistant.

Upstream: https://github.com/open-jarvis/OpenJarvis (Apache License 2.0)
Base commit: 93c1f87ab65e22cdd442a27da1e22aaf6f6b301e
Apply from the root of an OpenJarvis checkout at that commit:
    git apply ../patches/openjarvis-local.patch

What it changes (see NOTICE):
- sdk.py: Jarvis.ask() accepts `history` with earlier conversation turns.
- channels/telegram.py: voice notes and audio files reach handlers as bytes
  (metadata["audio"]); callbacks are coroutines, as python-telegram-bot expects.
- agents/morning_digest.py: Portuguese (pt-BR) briefing prompt, markdown
  stripping, money spoken as words ("R$ 55" -> "55 reais"), single generation.
- tools/digest_collect.py: cleaner email previews (no HTML, links or invisible
  padding), sender display names, merged duplicate emails, a one-day calendar
  horizon, Windows-safe date formatting, configurable items per source.
- core/config.py, system/orchestrator.py: digest `language`,
  `max_items_per_source` and a digest-only `model`.
- tests for all of the above.

Test fixtures in this file use placeholder senders (example.com).

